{"name":"Gauzy Calico","hex":"#c8e1e9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gauzy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Resembling gauze; light, thin, translucent.","light; giving the effect of haze"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gauzy"},{"term":"calico","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A kind of rough cloth made from unbleached and not fully processed cotton, often printed with a bright pattern.","Ellipsis of calico cat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of calico or resembling the color of calico cloth, having a pattern of red and contrasting areas; variegated.","Having red, brunette, and blond hair colors, resembling the fur of a calico cat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calico"}],"entries":[{"title":"Calico","blocks":[{"text":"Calico is a heavy plain-woven textile made from unbleached, and often not fully processed, cotton. It may also contain unseparated husk parts. The fabric is coarser than muslin, but less coarse and thick than canvas or denim. It is still very cheap owing to its unfinished and undyed appearance."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Calico_Sample.JPG/330px-Calico_Sample.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Calico","wikidata":"Q1132695"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Calico_sample_Crum_%26_Co..jpg/330px-Calico_sample_Crum_%26_Co..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Calico_sample_Crum_%26_Co..jpg/330px-Calico_sample_Crum_%26_Co..jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sample of calico printed with a six-colour machine by Walter Crum & Co., from Frederick Crace Calvert, Dyeing and Calico Printing (1878)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACal